Chapter: RocTextListThroughFn
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: string list through function", case 21 in file order:

     { f = |lst| lst x = ["a", "b"] result = f(x) match result { [first, ..] => first, _ => "" } }

 and Roc expects "a".

 Case 17's shape with a TEXT element instead of an Integer one, and Roc keeps
 both. The distinction is the same one matrix case f exists for: Integer is
 the language's default, so an Integer element can be answered correctly by a
 backend that is merely defaulting. Text cannot.

 ADAPTATION worth naming: Roc's harness prints an inspected string WITH its
 quotes (`"a"`), Codex's `print-line-uni` prints the text itself. The
 `.expected` here is `a`, and that is a difference in the harness rather than
 in the answer.

Section: Functions

  ident-text : List Text -> List Text
  ident-text (lst) = lst

  through : Integer -> Text
  through (n) =
   let x = ["a", "b"]
   in let result = ident-text x
   in list-at result 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (through 0)
  end
